    "description": "AEP Indiana Michigan Transmission Company, Inc. is a FERC-regulated transmission-only utility operating in Indiana and Michigan within PJM. The company owns high-voltage transmission lines and substations and is operated through American Electric Power affiliates rather than as a retail electric utility. Midwest Transmission Holdings, LLC owns the operating company directly; AEP holds an 80.1% economic interest and Olympus BidCo holds 19.9%. KKR and PSP Investments own Olympus 50/50, giving each a 9.95% look-through interest from the June 5, 2025 closing. AEP Ohio Transmission Company is a separate operating company and is not merged into this record.",
